# GMP credentials for gmp.sh. Copy to .gmp.env, edit, then: chmod 600 .gmp.env
#
# Use a DEDICATED low-privilege GMP user, never the Greenbone 'admin' account. It needs only
# enough rights to modify the one credential object, and to start and read the tasks you scan
# with. You must create this GMP user yourself (gvmd --create-user, or via GSA);
# bootstrap/Initialize-GvmScanCredential.ps1 creates the CREDENTIAL OBJECT, not the user.
#
# This file is the single place the GMP password lives, and only root reads it: the relay that
# reads it runs as root, while the stub the scan account invokes holds nothing. It must be 0600.

# Either naming works; GMP_USER/GMP_PASS is what an existing deployment may already use.
GMP_USER=scan-automation
GMP_PASS=change-me
